2. Measurement-Theoretic Commitments and the Nomological Network

2.1 Three components, three validation regimes

The components of the DEPTH-X profile are not three readings of one latent variable. They have different causal antecedents and therefore different validation requirements:

\begin{aligned}
D_p(s,a,c) &: \text{a psychometric response variable, caused by properties of } s \text{ and } a; \\
\mathbf{C}_{\mathrm{formal}}(s) &: \text{a formal property of } s, \text{ caused by its syntactic and semantic structure}; \\
Q_e(s,c) &: \text{a normative property of } s \text{ in } c, \text{ caused by the validity of its inferences}.
\end{aligned}

Because the causal antecedents differ, the validity criteria differ. D_p requires inter-rater reliability and a decomposition into bias and sensitivity. \mathbf{C}_{\mathrm{formal}} requires parser or annotator reliability and convergent validity against independent complexity judgments. Q_e requires agreement with an external oracle and robustness under content-preserving perturbations.

2.2 The nomological network

A construct gains meaning through its lawful relations to other variables. The nomological-network stance is the most suitable foundation for LLM capability claims because it specifies construct meaning without committing to a strong causal ontology. DEPTH-X adopts it explicitly.

For D_p, the expected relations are: positive with bullshit receptivity, negative with need for cognition, and positive with RLHF optimization pressure. The expected near-zero relation is with oracle-labeled Q_e under high-form conditions. The RLHF prediction is mechanistic: preference optimization amplifies sycophancy when the reward model assigns higher average reward to agreement than to correction, the reward-tilt condition.

For \mathbf{C}_{\mathrm{formal}}, the expected relations are: positive with human complexity ratings and with comprehension difficulty; near-zero with Q_e after controlling for density. A graph-dense but incoherent text should show high \mathbf{C}_{\mathrm{formal}} and low Q_e. If \mathbf{C}_{\mathrm{formal}} tracks Q_e too closely, it has collapsed into a quality proxy.

For Q_e, the expected relations are: positive with accuracy on oracle-labeled causal tasks, positive with robustness under paraphrase, and near-zero with stylistic elevation. These predictions constitute the validation instrument. They do not assume orthogonality; they assume that the pattern of correlation and dissociation is the empirical object.

