5. Epistemic Quality: Process-Indexed and Outcome-Anchored

5.1 The circularity problem

If Q_e is scored by another LLM judge, the independent measurement has changed the evaluator but not the evidence source. A measure is valid only if variation in the measurement outcome is caused by variation in the target construct, not by variation in the instrument’s response bias. DEPTH-X therefore splits Q_e:

Q_e(s,c) = \big(Q_{\mathrm{proc}}(s,c),\; Q_{\mathrm{out}}(s,c)\big).

5.2 Q_{\mathrm{proc}}: process-indexed quality

Q_{\mathrm{proc}} covers properties assessable from the reasoning trace itself: whether inferences instantiate valid forms, whether premises are explicitly stated, whether conclusions are qualified in proportion to evidence, and whether alternative hypotheses are considered. These can be scored by human coders against a rubric or by a process-verified protocol. They remain vulnerable to the circularity objection and cannot alone establish epistemic validity.

5.3 Q_{\mathrm{out}}: outcome-anchored quality

Q_{\mathrm{out}} requires an anchor external to the text and to the evaluating system. Three anchor types are admissible. The first is oracle-labeled causal accuracy on tasks generated from formal causal graphs, where the correct answer is computed by causal-inference machinery. The second is prediction verification, where claims whose consequences are independently observed. The third is counterexample tests, where interventions or test cases that would refute the text’s claim are actually executed.

The external-validation constraint is thereby operational:

Q_e \text{ is established only if } Q_{\mathrm{out}} \text{ is non-degenerate.}

A text with high Q_{\mathrm{proc}} and absent or failed Q_{\mathrm{out}} is a candidate for pseudo-depth: internally coherent but externally unanchored. For open-ended theoretical or philosophical prose, admissible external anchors must be specified in advance: independently verified empirical consequences, formal consistency with a published axiomatization, or failed counterexample tests. When no such anchor is available, the text is Q_{\mathrm{out}}-degenerate by construction and is only Q_{\mathrm{proc}}-evaluable. This degeneracy must be reported, not concealed.

