Prefatory note on the status of what follows. No experiments, physical tests, or code training were conducted for this chapter. Accordingly, no appendix reports data, pilot results, or estimated parameters. The derivations below are of three kinds only: (i) internal formal results, proved from the framework’s own definitions; (ii) standard statistical results, restated and derived in the notation of this chapter so that the design commitments are auditable; and (iii) cited theorems, stated with their scope conditions and attributed, but not reproved. Where a claim depends on an unexecuted procedure—most notably the systematic review—this is stated explicitly rather than assumed. “Proof” in these appendices therefore never means empirical confirmation.

